    changelog.md
        1→## v0.6.4
        3→### Fixes
        5→- Remove `any` in command line options.
        6→- XML: Handle empty nodes containing fields correctly. (#121)
        8→## v0.6.3
        10→### Features
        12→Enhanced automatic Content Type detection. Even when users don't provide file extensions, otree can now automatically detect the ContentType based on the data content.
        14→For example, the following command is now available:
        16→```bash
        17→echo '{"key": "value"}' | otree
        18→```
        20→Now otree will try invoking all parsers in order for unknown content, and whichever parser succeeds determines the format.
        22→## v0.6.2
        24→### Features
        26→- Data block now support wrap mode, this will disable horizontal scrolling, and
        27→  long text will be split to a new line. You can enable this by `--wrap` or
        28→  `-w` command line option. To change the default behavior, add `data.wrap = true` in config file. (#104)
        97→## v0.5.1
        99→### Fixes
        101→- Fix panic when using action `expand_children` for empty object. (#87)
        111→## v0.4.1
        113→### Features
        115→- when copying values, use pure text. (#80)
        117→## v0.4.0
        119→### Features
        121→- Command: Add new flag `--debug`, to write some debug logs to a file.
        122→- UI: Add `--live-reload` option, to watch file changes and update tui (#63).
        123→- Release: Add Windows prebuilt binary (**unstable**, require more testing).
        125→## v0.3.0
        127→### Features
        129→- Parser: Support [JSONL](https://jsonlines.org/)
        130→- README: Add Homebrew instructions.
        132→### Fixes
        134→- Allow reading from stdin on macOS.
        151→## v0.1.0
        153→### Features
        155→- Basic tree and data UI.
        156→- Basic actions, see: [actions](./actions.md).
